      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense, I will add that check in.\n\nfollow-up:\nChecking for `kIsConverter` in the  flags causes identity/no-op converts to fail, i.e.\n```convert: No defined conversion from \u0027u32\u0027 to \u0027u32\u0027``\n\nShould cases like this be failing validation? (i.e. should the transforms be making sure they actually need to do a convert)\n\nIf no-op cases should pass, the easiest fix is probably to add an early check for if val type and result type are the same.",
